{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>She shall bring a lamb.</b> His disciples asked Rabbi Shimon bar Yochai: why did the Torah say that a woman who gives birth brings an offering? He said to them: at the moment she crouches to give birth, she cries out and swears that she will never again have relations with her husband. Therefore the Torah said: she shall bring an offering." "<b>[In its year.</b> Within its year.] <b>Unto the entrance of the Tent of Meeting.</b> This teaches that she attends to them until the entrance of the Tent of Meeting."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:11:36.999605824Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}